Gears of War 3: DLSS / FSR at 2x internal resolution, and the HUD kept out of the upscaler. The
scene depth was taken only when it was exactly the guest frame size (a filter against larger shadow
maps), so at 2x the 2560x1440 depth was never used and every frame went out without the upscaler.
A depth texture now matches when it is the guest size times a whole scale. The UI mask rectangles
are guest pixels; they are scaled to the render size, or at 2x the mask covered only the top-left
quarter of the frame. Inside the mask the presented image is now the game's own frame (bilinear
when upscaling): the mask only biased the upscaler, which still sharpened and lightened HUD text.
Traced frames (gow2_trace.now) log the mask rectangles (UIMASK) and each UI draw's estimate
(UIDRAW).

